MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me and PTXmas fit the Christmas listening reflected in several of my recent choices, so both felt worth considering.",
    "The vocal harmonies of That's Christmas To Me also connect with what appeals to me about The New Old Fashioned, making it my strongest choice on this visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Summer Horns and Amazing 50s Stereo Jukebox offer summer-themed music or general oldies, which do not meet my current desire for Christmas vocals.",
    "Duets, solo pop, country retrospectives, and film-related recordings do not become appealing just because they are music; I need a clearer connection to the holiday mood or vocal-group sound I want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seemed to treat an interest in familiar songs and traditional sounds as a broad interest in oldies and retrospective collections.",
    "They also seemed to treat different kinds of vocal recordings as interchangeable, although a duets collection or solo singer does not give me the same appeal as vocal-group harmonies."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several Christmas recordings chosen close together suggest a focused listening interest that deserves more weight than a loose connection to music in general.",
    "My later choice of The New Old Fashioned adds an interest in vocal-group arrangements; combining that with my Christmas choices explains why That's Christmas To Me stands out."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in Christmas vocals but stretched it too broadly into unrelated familiar music."
}
